<p><strong>Market selection criteria:</strong><br />
- 50 US cities ranging from 100,000 to 2+ million population<br />
- Mix of competitive markets (Dallas, Phoenix, Atlanta) and mid-tier markets (Boise, Richmond, Omaha)<br />
- At least one city per Census region (Northeast, Midwest, South, West)<br />
- Excluded markets where a single directory or lead-gen site dominated the local pack</p>
<p><strong>Profile selection criteria:</strong><br />
- Active GBP with visible address or defined service area<br />
- At least 6 months of activity (to avoid brand-new profiles with artificial signals)<br />
- No suspended or penalized profiles<br />
- Mix of ranking positions (positions 1-20 in local pack)</p>
<h3>Variables Analyzed</h3>
<p>For each profile, we recorded:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Primary category</strong> (exact text)</li>
<li><strong>Secondary categories count</strong></li>
<li><strong>Review count</strong> (total)</li>
<li><strong>Review rating</strong> (average stars)</li>
<li><strong>Review velocity</strong> (new reviews per month, calculated from visible timeline)</li>
<li><strong>Review recency</strong> (days since most recent review)</li>
<li><strong>Photo count</strong> (total uploaded)</li>
<li><strong>Photo recency</strong> (days since most recent photo)</li>
<li><strong>Post frequency</strong> (posts per month)</li>
<li><strong>Q&amp;A count</strong> (questions + answers)</li>
<li><strong>Business description length</strong> (character count)</li>
<li><strong>Service area size</strong> (number of cities/ZIPs defined)</li>
<li><strong>Website link presence</strong> (yes/no)</li>
<li><strong>Business hours completeness</strong> (full week vs. partial)</li>
<li><strong>Attributes completion</strong> (percentage of available attributes filled)</li>
<li><strong>Products/services listed</strong> (yes/no)</li>
</ol>
<h3>Ranking Measurement</h3>
<p>We measured local pack position for each profile using this query pattern:</p>
<div class="code-block">
<pre><code>[trade] + [city] + &quot;near me&quot;
</code></pre>
</div>
<p>Examples: "roofing contractor Dallas near me," "HVAC repair Phoenix near me."</p>
<p><strong>Measurement protocol:</strong><br />
- Searches conducted from IP addresses within each target metro area<br />
- Incognito browser sessions, cleared cache/cookies<br />
- Mobile viewport (375px width) to match dominant local search behavior<br />
- Searches conducted between 9 AM and 5 PM local time on weekdays<br />
- Each query run three times; position recorded as median value<br />
- Local Services Ads excluded from position count</p>
<h3>Statistical Approach</h3>
<p>We used <strong>Spearman rank correlation</strong> to measure relationships between each variable and ranking position. Spearman is appropriate here because:<br />
- Ranking positions are ordinal, not continuous<br />
- It handles non-linear relationships (common in local SEO)<br />
- It's robust to outliers (e.g., a profile with 2,000 reviews)</p>
<p>Correlation coefficients range from -1 (perfect negative correlation: higher variable = better ranking) to +1 (perfect positive correlation: higher variable = worse ranking). A coefficient of 0 means no relationship.</p>
<p><strong>Interpretation guide:</strong></p>
<div class="cost-table">
