<h2>Key Finding #2: Photo Quantity Shows Stronger Correlation Than Expected</h2>
<p><strong>The data:</strong> Photo count correlated at <strong>-0.35</strong> with ranking position — stronger than review count (-0.22) and nearly as strong as review recency (-0.41).</p>
<p>This surprised us. The SEO industry has long treated GBP photos as a "nice to have" rather than a ranking driver. Google's own statements suggest photos are primarily an engagement signal, not a direct ranking factor. But the correlation in our data is too strong to ignore.</p>
