<h2>Key Finding #3: Primary Category Selection Is the Single Highest-Impact Variable</h2>
<p><strong>The data:</strong> Primary category alignment showed the strongest correlation of any variable we measured: <strong>-0.47</strong>.</p>
<p>This wasn't a numerical variable — it was a binary classification. We scored each profile's primary category as either "aligned" (directly matching the search query intent) or "misaligned" (a broader or tangential category).</p>
