<h2>Key Finding #5: Service-Area Businesses Face a Structural Disadvantage (But Can Overcome It)</h2>
<p><strong>The data:</strong> Service-area businesses (SABs) with hidden addresses ranked in positions 1-3 <strong>31% less often</strong> than brick-and-mortar contractors with visible addresses — <strong>when all other variables were equal</strong>.</p>
<p>This is the most controversial finding in our study. It suggests that hiding your address, while often necessary for compliance, may carry a ranking penalty.</p>
