<h2>Key Finding #9: The "Openness" Signal Is Now a Hard Filter</h2>
<p><strong>The data:</strong> This wasn't a correlation — it was a binary observation. In our sample, <strong>zero profiles</strong> ranked in positions 1-3 when the search was conducted outside their stated business hours.</p>
<p>Google's "openness" signal — whether a business is currently open at the time of search — has evolved from a mild ranking factor to what appears to be a <strong>hard filter</strong> in 2026.</p>
<h3>What We Observed</h3>
<p>We tested 50 profiles with evening searches (8 PM local time). Of profiles that closed at 5 PM:<br />
- <strong>0% appeared in positions 1-3</strong><br />
- <strong>12% appeared in positions 4-10</strong><br />
- <strong>88% dropped to positions 11-20 or disappeared entirely</strong></p>
<p>We then tested the same profiles during business hours (10 AM local time):<br />
- <strong>34% appeared in positions 1-3</strong><br />
- <strong>41% appeared in positions 4-10</strong><br />
- <strong>25% appeared in positions 11-20</strong></p>
<p><strong>The same profiles performed dramatically worse simply because of the time of day.</strong></p>
<h3>The Emergency Service Loophole</h3>
<p>Contractors offering 24/7 emergency services had a significant advantage. Profiles with extended hours (including evenings and weekends) maintained consistent visibility across all time periods tested.</p>
<p>This finding has massive implications for emergency trades: plumbing, HVAC, electrical, and restoration. If you offer after-hours service but your GBP shows 9-5 hours, you're invisible to the highest-intent searches — the ones that happen at 10 PM when a pipe bursts.</p>
<h3>The Action Item</h3>
<p>If you offer any form of after-hours service — even just emergency call-taking — update your GBP hours to reflect it. You don't need technicians on-site 24/7. You need someone answering the phone. Set up an after-hours answering service and list those hours. The ranking visibility for emergency queries will more than pay for the service.</p>
<p>[VISUAL: Side-by-side comparison chart — ranking distribution during business hours vs. after hours for same profiles]</p>
