<h2>What This Means for Your GBP Strategy</h2>
<p>Let's translate these findings into a prioritized action plan.</p>
<h3>Tier 1: Do These First (Highest Impact)</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Audit your primary category.</strong> If it doesn't exactly match your core service, change it today.</li>
<li><strong>Implement a review generation system.</strong> Target 4-8 new reviews per month with automated requests within 24 hours of job completion.</li>
<li><strong>Upload 60+ photos</strong> across all categories, then add 2-3 new photos weekly.</li>
</ol>
<h3>Tier 2: Do These Next (Strong Impact)</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Post twice per week</strong> on your GBP with project updates, seasonal tips, and offers.</li>
<li><strong>Respond to 100% of reviews</strong> within 24-48 hours using keyword-rich, personalized replies.</li>
<li><strong>Select exactly 3 secondary categories</strong> — remove any tangential ones.</li>
</ol>
<h3>Tier 3: Do These When Tier 1-2 Are Complete (Moderate Impact)</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Update business hours</strong> to reflect any after-hours or emergency service availability.</li>
<li><strong>Tighten your service area</strong> to specific cities rather than a broad radius.</li>
<li><strong>Write a concise business description</strong> (150-300 characters) with your primary service and top locations.</li>
<li><strong>Complete all available attributes</strong> in your GBP.</li>
</ol>
<h3>What NOT to Waste Time On</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Lengthy business descriptions</strong> — 300 characters is plenty</li>
<li><strong>GBP Q&amp;A</strong> — Google is removing this feature</li>
<li><strong>Adding 8+ secondary categories</strong> — 3 is the sweet spot</li>
<li><strong>Bulk photo uploads</strong> — consistent freshness beats one-time volume</li>
<li><strong>Keyword-stuffing your business name</strong> — this triggers suspensions and penalties</li>
</ul>
