<h2>Limitations of This Study</h2>
<p>We believe in transparent methodology — including honest acknowledgment of what this study cannot tell you.</p>
<h3>1. Correlation Is Not Causation</h3>
<p>A strong correlation between photo count and ranking position might mean photos cause better rankings. Or it might mean successful businesses simply have more resources to upload photos. We cannot prove causation from observational data.</p>
<h3>2. Proximity Is a Confounding Variable</h3>
<p>Google's local algorithm weighs proximity heavily — often more heavily than any factor we measured. A perfectly optimized profile 20 miles from the searcher may still lose to a mediocre profile 2 miles away. Our study controlled for this by searching from within each metro area, but we could not fully isolate proximity effects.</p>
<h3>3. Industry-Specific Generalization</h3>
<p>Our sample includes only contractors in six home service trades. These findings may not generalize to restaurants, retail, healthcare, or professional services. Each industry has unique competitive dynamics.</p>
<h3>4. Temporal Validity</h3>
<p>Google's algorithm changes constantly. The ranking factor weights we observed in February 2026 may shift by summer. The Q&amp;A deprecation is one example of how quickly the landscape changes.</p>
<h3>5. Sample Size by Trade</h3>
<p>While 500 total profiles is substantial, individual trades had samples of 72-95 profiles. This is adequate for correlation analysis but limits our ability to detect subtle trade-specific effects.</p>
<h3>6. Ranking Position Measurement</h3>
<p>Local pack rankings vary by searcher location, device, search history, and time of day. We standardized our measurement protocol, but some variance is inevitable. We report median positions from three searches to reduce noise.</p>
<h3>7. Missing Variables</h3>
<p>We did not measure:<br />
- Website quality and on-page SEO<br />
- Backlink profiles<br />
- Citation consistency<br />
- Google Ads / Local Services Ads spend<br />
- Historical ranking trajectory<br />
- Brand search volume</p>
<p>These factors almost certainly influence rankings and may explain some of the variance our model didn't capture.</p>
